<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android dependencies for the Layers Unity SDK, resolved by the External
  Dependency Manager for Unity (EDM4U). This is the same mechanism Firebase,
  AppsFlyer, Adjust and Google's own Unity packages use.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-04): it did not, and the package shipped no
  Android dependency mechanism of any kind — no Dependencies.xml, no
  .androidlib, no Gradle template. Meanwhile AndroidModule.cs reaches both of
  these libraries by JNI class lookup:

    AndroidModule.cs:77   com.google.android.gms.ads.identifier.AdvertisingIdClient
    AndroidModule.cs:170  com.android.installreferrer.api.InstallReferrerClient

  Neither is on a stock Unity project's Android classpath, so both lookups
  always failed: the Google Advertising ID and the Play install referrer —
  Android's install-attribution channel — could never resolve for any game
  using this package. The failures are silent, which is why it was invisible.

  play-services-ads-identifier's own AAR manifest declares
  <uses-permission android:name="com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID"/>,
  which Android 13+ / targetSdk 33+ requires to read the GAID at all, so that
  permission merges into the built app transitively with this dependency
  rather than needing to be declared separately. Declaring it separately would
  also be wrong: an app that resolves no advertising ID should not request the
  permission, since Play Console data-safety answers must match.

  Versions match the Kotlin and Flutter SDK pins so a project embedding more
  than one Layers surface cannot end up resolving two Play Services majors.

  REQUIRES EDM4U. Without it installed in the consuming project this file is
  inert and the two features stay unavailable — it cannot break a build, but it
  cannot help either. See unity/README.md for the install link.
-->
<dependencies>
  <androidPackages>
    <androidPackage spec="com.google.android.gms:play-services-ads-identifier:18.1.0" />
    <androidPackage spec="com.android.installreferrer:installreferrer:2.2" />
  </androidPackages>
</dependencies>
